{"id": "EUVD-2026-58955", "enisaUuid": "20eda288-7004-39b1-b1ab-e50a5390c534", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs/ntfs3: bound DeleteIndexEntryAllocation memmove length\n\nIn do_action()'s DeleteIndexEntryAllocation case, e->size comes\nfrom an on-disk INDEX_BUFFER entry.  When e->size makes\ne + e->size point past hdr + hdr->used,\nPtrOffset(e1, Add2Ptr(hdr, used)) returns a negative ptrdiff_t\nthat is silently cast to a quasi-infinite size_t when passed\nto memmove().  The memmove then walks past the destination\nbuffer.\n\nThe sibling DeleteIndexEntryRoot case at fslog.c:3540-3543\nalready carries the corresponding guard:\n\n\tif (PtrOffset(e1, Add2Ptr(hdr, used)) < esize ||\n\t    Add2Ptr(e, esize) > Add2Ptr(lrh, rec_len) ||\n\t    used + esize > le32_to_cpu(hdr->total)) {\n\t\tgoto dirty_vol;\n\t}\n\nApply the same shape to the allocation-path case.  Also reject\nesize == 0: memmove(e, e, ...) is a no-op and leaves\nhdr->used unchanged, hiding a malformed entry from the\nexisting check_index_header() walk.\n\nReproduced under UML+KASAN on mainline 8d90b09e6741 by\nmounting a crafted NTFS image: the unguarded memmove takes a\nlength of 0xffffffffffffff00 and the kernel oopses in\nmemmove+0x81/0x1a0 on the do_action+0x36a2 frame.\n\n[almaz.alexandrovich@paragon-software.com: clang-formatted the changes]", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:53:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:45:01", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c38ed2ab62fab75fd6d0fdc2bee540fbebc7b959", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b509b9613f20dc5b653d54bf78fab00d79cc43c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c8aac931c1cd70347961ba5157aa916448c6a25", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f383aae59ec3994c14804f4191c59038b206be81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09fddd52c1b0cef2c086d61be8f3d5dc92e36565", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/554700c65d398276cb00a8ef95f1d5e00b9eff93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc4626bb3656362de8b0ecd56605d47a19ec3518"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72197", "GHSA-j9fv-qm2v-gr26"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0513968f-3d2b-3301-bc9f-2f5a1292ed7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <554700c65d398276cb00a8ef95f1d5e00b9eff93"}, {"id": "05541e70-348b-3c95-ad25-222c68e82806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <4c8aac931c1cd70347961ba5157aa916448c6a25"}, {"id": "13ca2129-32de-3b49-aa98-9d847deecaee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "3f1db22a-1feb-336e-9b85-1c3972bb18cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "4eeb7406-2362-34c3-af40-ec0460e18de9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "4fbbff9a-6092-3486-a054-f2330dd4e85d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "6983ac04-2a91-3945-845a-6bdefafccc21", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "72241a1a-08e8-38b7-8e2e-fbf874ba4610", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d876898e1c84d3f84902264b445 <fc4626bb3656362de8b0ecd56605d47a19ec3518"}, {"id": "77f69910-28d9-36da-a18a-b68d210f6e23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "b939f519-bd69-3257-a088-6a901b786120", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "ca6d2618-cfee-3f12-897b-90346a66ea1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b46acd6a6a627d